S = 3`, `BACKOFF_SECONDS = [1, 4, 16]`.\n        - Fix direction: introduce an idempotency key reused across attempts; must be persisted so restarts reuse it (durable storage, e.g., on charge/job record).\n        - Tests previously: `pytest payments/worker/tests -q` => `48 passed`.\n        - Refunds worker previously had same problematic pattern: `refunds/worker/retry.py` used bare `continue` on `TimeoutError` (was edited to address; needs verification/tests).\n        - Runbook updated: payments runbook documents idempotency key lifetime and restart behavior.\n        - New instrumentation requirement implemented: counter metric `payments.retry.key_reused` emitted when a retry reuses an existing idempotency key (from `submit_with_retry`).\n    </key_knowledge>\n\n    <artifact_trail>\n        - `payments/worker/retry.py`: Previously modified to add idempotency behavior to prevent double-charge on retry after `TimeoutError` while keeping API shape unchanged (exact content not captured). Subsequently edited again (+6/-1) to emit a metric when a retry reuses an existing idempotency key (counter `payments.retry.key_reused` from `submit_with_retry`).\n        - `payments/worker/tests/test_retry.py`: Added regression test `test_no_duplicate_on_timeout` to ensure timeout-then-retry does not double-submit/charge.\n        - `refunds/worker/retry.py`: Edited earlier (net +11/-2) to address analogous `TimeoutError` retry issue; exact final behavior not captured; requires verification and tests.\n        - `docs/runbooks/payments.md`: Edited (+24/-0) to document idempotency key usage, lifetime, and restart behavior.\n    </artifact_trail>\n\n    <file_system_state>\n        - Relevant paths (touched/known):\n          - MODIFIED: `payments/worker/retry.py` (idempotency + metric emission; latest edit +6/-1)\n          - CREATED/MODIFIED: `payments/worker/tests/test_retry.py` (added `test_no_duplicate_on_timeout`)\n          - MODIFIED: `refunds/worker/retry.py` (retry safety