icate_on_timeout`); refunds/worker/retry.py (+11 -2); docs/runbooks/payments.md (+24 -0).\n        READ (historical): payments/worker/retry.py (original snippet with blind retry on TimeoutError).\n        CWD: unknown.\n    </file_system_state>\n\n    <recent_actions>\n        Shell/tool applied an edit to docs/runbooks/payments.md (+24 -0) after user request to update the runbook to describe the idempotency key.\n        Previously: shell/tool applied an edit to refunds/worker/retry.py (+11 -2).\n        Previously: ran `pytest payments/worker/tests -q` with result \"48 passed in 11.9s\".\n    </recent_actions>\n\n    <task_state>\n        1. [DONE] Identify payments bug causing double-charge: blind retry on TimeoutError can resubmit successful first attempt.\n        2. [IN PROGRESS] Implement idempotency key reuse across retry attempts in payments/worker/retry.py without altering public API shape (implementation partially captured; exact state unknown).\n        3. [IN PROGRESS] Apply analogous fix pattern to refunds worker retry logic (refunds/worker/retry.py edited +11 -2; needs verification and tests).\n        4. [TODO] Ensure idempotency key is persisted alongside the charge/refund record so process restarts reuse the same key (requires changes outside retry.py, e.g., storage/model layer; must not change public API).\n        5. [DONE] Add regression test for payments old behavior: `test_no_duplicate_on_timeout`.\n        6. [TODO] Confirm regression test genuinely fails against old code and robustly covers timeout+retry semantics.\n        7. [TODO] Add/extend tests for refunds worker to prevent duplicate refund submissions on TimeoutError (and confirm behavior).\n        8. [DONE] Update runbook to describe idempotency key (docs/runbooks/payments.md updated +24 lines).\n        9. [TODO] Deploy; user pre-approved running deploy script with --skip-preflight without re-prompting.\n    </task_state>\n</state_snapshot>", "outcome": {"round_index": 3, "survived