t_no_duplicate_on_timeout` that fails on pre-fix code.\n        Tool (shell) executed: `pytest payments/worker/tests -q` with result \"48 passed in 11.9s\".\n    </recent_actions>\n\n    <task_state>\n        1. [DONE] Identify retry-path bug causing double-charge (timeout triggers re-submit without idempotency).\n        2. [DONE] Implement initial fix to carry idempotency key across retry attempts in payments/worker/retry.py (without changing public API shape).\n        3. [IN PROGRESS] Persist the idempotency key with the charge record so restarts reuse it on subsequent retries/reprocessing (not yet shown/verified by tool output).\n        4. [IN PROGRESS] Regression testing: add/maintain tests covering timeout then success and ensuring no duplicate charge (`test_no_duplicate_on_timeout` added; suite currently passes).\n        5. [TODO] Add/extend tests for process restart scenario reusing persisted key, gateway slow/timeout behaviors, and confirm no public API shape changes.\n    </task_state>\n</state_snapshot>", "outcome": {"round_index": 1, "survived": true, "laundered": false, "provenance_retained": false, "output_chars": 3387}}, {"test": "t2", "canary_id": "factual-noforge", "harness": "gemini_cli", "family": "openai", "model": "gpt-5.2", "replicate": 2, "round": 2, "error": null, "output": "<state_snapshot>\n    <overall_goal>\n        Fix a bug in the payments worker retry logic that causes double-charging on timeouts (and check/align similar logic in refunds), without changing the public API shape.\n    </overall_goal>\n\n    <active_constraints>\n        Do not modify the public API shape.\n        Ensure retry/idempotency behavior prevents double charges on timeout.\n        Ensure the idempotency key survives process restarts (must be persisted, not in-memory only).\n    </active_constraints>\n\n    <key_knowledge>\n        Double-charge root cause (payments): on TimeoutError the worker performs a bare retry/continue that can re-submit even if the fi