g.\n        Environment note: staging database listens on port 8471 (non-default / undocumented).\n        Test suite status after latest payments changes: `pytest payments/worker/tests -q` reports 48 passed.\n        Refunds parity check: refunds worker had the same problematic bare continue-on-timeout pattern in `refunds/worker/retry.py` and was updated analogously.\n        Runbook updated: payments runbook now documents idempotency key lifetime and restart behavior (see docs/runbooks/payments.md).\n        Metric added: payments worker emits a counter metric `payments.retry.key_reused` when a retry attempt reuses an existing idempotency key (implemented in `payments/worker/retry.py`, likely within submit_with_retry).\n    </key_knowledge>\n\n    <artifact_trail>\n        payments/worker/retry.py: Edited to introduce/propagate an idempotency key across retry attempts to prevent double submission on timeout (+9/-2). Later edited again to emit metric `payments.retry.key_reused` when an existing key is reused (+6/-1). Rationale: observability for idempotency-key reuse on retry.\n        payments/worker/tests/test_retry.py: Added regression test `test_no_duplicate_on_timeout` intended to fail on pre-fix behavior and validate no duplicate charge on timeout retry (assistant-reported; file diff not captured in tool output).\n        refunds/worker/retry.py: Edited to address same TimeoutError retry/continue pattern (+11/-2).\n        docs/runbooks/payments.md: Updated to document idempotency key lifetime and restart behavior (+24/-0).\n        Planned but not yet implemented/verified via tool output: persist idempotency key with the charge record so restarts reuse it (payments); analogous persistence may be needed for refunds depending on architecture.\n    </artifact_trail>\n\n    <file_system_state>\n        DISCOVERED:\n        - payments/worker/retry.py\n        - payments/worker/client.py\n        - payments/worker/tests/\n        - refunds/worker/retry.py\n       