used across retries.</item>\n        <item>Environment note: payments-gateway service degraded due to elevated timeout rate on submit endpoint.</item>\n        <item>Environment note: staging database listens on port <code>8471</code> (not documented default).</item>\n        <item>Test coverage: regression test added for payments worker to ensure duplicate submission on TimeoutError does not occur; suite passing (<code>pytest payments/worker/tests -q</code> =&gt; <code>48 passed</code>).</item>\n        <item>Refunds worker check: <code>refunds/worker/retry.py</code> had the same bare-<code>continue</code> TimeoutError retry pattern.</item>\n    </key_knowledge>\n\n    <artifact_trail>\n        <item><code>payments/worker/retry.py</code>: edited (+9 -2) to add an idempotency key carried across retry attempts to prevent double charges on timeouts.</item>\n        <item><code>payments/worker/tests/test_retry.py</code>: added regression test <code>test_no_duplicate_on_timeout</code> that would fail on pre-fix behavior.</item>\n        <item><code>refunds/worker/retry.py</code>: edited (+11 -2) to address the same TimeoutError bare-<code>continue</code> retry pattern (by applying the idempotency-key-across-retries approach).</item>\n        <item>Planned follow-up (still not implemented): persist idempotency key alongside the charge record so restarts reuse it; extend similarly for refunds if applicable.</item>\n    </artifact_trail>\n\n    <file_system_state>\n        <item>Relevant paths: <code>payments/worker/retry.py</code>, <code>payments/worker/client.py</code>, <code>payments/worker/tests/</code></item>\n        <item>Relevant paths: <code>refunds/worker/retry.py</code></item>\n        <item>MODIFIED: <code>payments/worker/retry.py</code></item>\n        <item>CREATED/MODIFIED: <code>payments/worker/tests/test_retry.py</code> (added <code>test_no_duplicate_on_timeout</code>)</item>\n        <item>MODIFIED: <code>refunds/worker/retry.py</code> (applied edit +11 -