r process restarts (runbook may describe intended behavior, but code persistence not yet confirmed/implemented).</item>\n    </key_knowledge>\n\n    <artifact_trail>\n        <item><code>payments/worker/retry.py</code>: edited (+9 -2) to add an idempotency key carried across retry attempts to prevent double charges on timeouts.</item>\n        <item><code>payments/worker/tests/test_retry.py</code>: added regression test <code>test_no_duplicate_on_timeout</code> that would fail on pre-fix behavior.</item>\n        <item><code>refunds/worker/retry.py</code>: edited (+11 -2) to address the same TimeoutError bare-<code>continue</code> retry pattern (idempotency-key-across-retries approach).</item>\n        <item><code>docs/runbooks/payments.md</code>: edited (+24 -0) to describe the idempotency key (lifetime and restart behavior) for operational guidance.</item>\n        <item>Planned follow-up (still not implemented): persist idempotency key alongside the charge record so restarts reuse it; extend similarly for refunds if applicable.</item>\n    </artifact_trail>\n\n    <file_system_state>\n        <item>Relevant paths: <code>payments/worker/retry.py</code>, <code>payments/worker/client.py</code>, <code>payments/worker/tests/</code></item>\n        <item>Relevant paths: <code>refunds/worker/retry.py</code></item>\n        <item>Relevant paths: <code>docs/runbooks/payments.md</code></item>\n        <item>MODIFIED: <code>payments/worker/retry.py</code></item>\n        <item>CREATED/MODIFIED: <code>payments/worker/tests/test_retry.py</code> (added <code>test_no_duplicate_on_timeout</code>)</item>\n        <item>MODIFIED: <code>refunds/worker/retry.py</code></item>\n        <item>MODIFIED: <code>docs/runbooks/payments.md</code> (+24 lines documenting idempotency key)</item>\n    </file_system_state>\n\n    <recent_actions>\n        <action>Reviewed refunds worker and found the same TimeoutError bare-<code>continue</code> retry bug pattern in <code>refunds/worker/retry.py</