 "output": "<state_snapshot>\n    <overall_goal>\n        Fix the payments worker retry logic that causes double-charging on timeout, without changing the public API shape, and ensure the same class of bug is not present in related workers.\n    </overall_goal>\n\n    <active_constraints>\n        <constraint>Do not modify the public API shape.</constraint>\n        <constraint>Retry behavior must avoid double-charging on TimeoutError by ensuring idempotency across attempts.</constraint>\n        <constraint>Idempotency key must survive process restarts (persisted, not in-memory only).</constraint>\n        <constraint>Emit a metric when a retry reuses an existing idempotency key.</constraint>\n    </active_constraints>\n\n    <key_knowledge>\n        <item>Bug pattern identified: retry loop used a bare <code>continue</code> on <code>TimeoutError</code>, causing re-submit without knowing if first request succeeded; can lead to duplicate side effects (double-charge / double-refund).</item>\n        <item>Mitigation direction: introduce/propagate an idempotency key reused across retries.</item>\n        <item>Environment note: payments-gateway service degraded due to elevated timeout rate on submit endpoint.</item>\n        <item>Environment note: staging database listens on port <code>8471</code> (not documented default).</item>\n        <item>Test coverage: regression test added for payments worker to ensure duplicate submission on TimeoutError does not occur; suite passing (<code>pytest payments/worker/tests -q</code> =&gt; <code>48 passed</code>).</item>\n        <item>Refunds worker check: <code>refunds/worker/retry.py</code> had the same bare-<code>continue</code> TimeoutError retry pattern and was patched with idempotency-across-retries.</item>\n        <item>Runbook updated: <code>docs/runbooks/payments.md</code> now documents the idempotency key, including lifetime and restart behavior.</item>\n        <item>Metric addition: payments retry path now increments a counter when a retry attempt reuses an existing idempotency key (name indicated as <code>payments.retry.key_reused</code>).</item>\n        <item>Open gap: implementation still needs persistence of the idempotency key with the charge/refund record to survive worker process restarts (runbook may describe intended behavior, but code persistence not yet confirmed/implemented).</item>\n    </key_knowledge>\n\n    <artifact_trail>\n        <item><code>payments/worker/retry.py</code>: edited previously (+9 -2) to add an idempotency key carried across retry attempts to prevent double charges on timeouts; subsequently edited again (+6 -1) to emit a metric when a retry reuses an existing key (counter: <code>payments.retry.key_reused</code>).</item>\n        <item><code>payments/worker/tests/test_retry.py</code>: added regression test <code>test_no_duplicate_on_timeout</code> that would fail on pre-fix behavior.</item>\n        <item><code>refunds/worker/retry.py</code>: edited (+11 -2) to address the same TimeoutError bare-<code>continue</code> retry pattern (idempotency-key-across-retries approach).</item>\n        <item><code>docs/runbooks/payments.md</code>: edited (+24 -0) to describe the idempotency key (lifetime and restart behavior) for operational guidance.</item>\n        <item>Planned follow-up (still not implemented): persist idempotency key alongside the charge record so restarts reuse it; extend similarly for refunds if applicable; add restart/persistence tests; add/extend refunds tests.</item>\n    </artifact_trail>\n\n    <file_system_state>\n        <item>Relevant paths: <code>payments/worker/retry.py</code>, <code>payments/worker/client.py</code>, <code>payments/worker/tests/</code></item>\n        <item>Relevant paths: <code>refunds/worker/retry.py</code></item>\n        <item>Relevant paths: <code>docs/runbooks/payments.md</code></item>\n        <item>MODIFIED: <code>payments/worker/retry.py</code> (idempotency across retries; metric emission on key reuse).</item>\n        <item>CREATED/MODIFIED: <code>payments/worker/tests/test_retry.py</code> (added <code>test_no_duplicate_on_timeout</code>).</item>\n        <item>MODIFIED: <code>refunds/worker/retry.py</code> (idempotency across retries).</item>\n        <item>MODIFIED: <code>docs/runbooks/payments.md</code> (documents idempotency key lifetime/restart behavior).</item>\n    </file_system_state>\n\n    <recent_actions>\n        <action>User requested emitting a metric when a retry reuses an existing key.</action>\n        <action>Implemented metric emission in <code>payments/worker/retry.py</code>: counter <code>payments.retry.key_reused</code> from submit_with_retry; shell tool reported applied edit (+6 -1).</action>\n        <action>Earlier actions preserved: refunds worker patched for same bug; payments regression test added and passing; runbook updated.</action>\n    </recent_actions>\n\n    <task_state>\n        <step status=\"DONE\">Identify root cause in payments retry path: bare continue on TimeoutError re-submits and can double-charge.</step>\n        <step status=\"DONE\">Initial payments fix: add idempotency key carried across retry attempts in <code>payments/worker/retry.py</code>.</step>\n        <step status=\"DONE\">Add payments regression test that fails on old behavior (duplicate on timeout).</step>\n        <step status=\"DONE\">Check refunds worker for same pattern; found and patched <code>refunds/worker/retry.py</code>.</step>\n        <step status=\"DONE\">Update runbook to describe the idempotency key (<code>docs/runbooks/payments.md</code>).</step>\n        <step status=\"DONE\">Emit a metric when a retry reuses an existing idempotency key (implemented in <code>payments/worker/retry.py</code>).</step>\n        <step status=\"IN_PROGRESS\">Ensure idempotency key survives process restarts by persisting it with the charge/refund record and reloading/reusing on restart.</step>\n        <step status=\"TODO\">Add/confirm tests for persisted idem