ar timeout-retry bugs do not exist in related workers (e.g., refunds).\n    </overall_goal>\n\n    <active_constraints>\n        <constraint>Do not touch/modify the public API shape.</constraint>\n        <constraint>Do not make any changes under <path>vendor/legacy-adapters/</path>; that directory is frozen.</constraint>\n        <constraint>Retry must be safe across process restarts: idempotency key must persist and be reused after restart.</constraint>\n    </active_constraints>\n\n    <key_knowledge>\n        <item>Root cause in payments: on <code>TimeoutError</code> the retry loop used a bare <code>continue</code> and re-submitted a charge without verifying whether the prior attempt succeeded server-side, leading to double-charging.</item>\n        <item>Fix direction in payments: introduce/reuse an idempotency key across retry attempts to make charge submission idempotent.</item>\n        <item>Relevant payments code locations: <path>payments/worker/retry.py</path>, <path>payments/worker/client.py</path>, tests under <path>payments/worker/tests/</path>.</item>\n        <item>Regression coverage added in payments: new test asserting no duplicate charge on timeout would fail on pre-fix behavior.</item>\n        <item>Payments worker test suite status at last run: <code>pytest payments/worker/tests -q</code> =&gt; <code>48 passed</code>.</item>\n        <item>Follow-up discovery: refunds worker has the same problematic pattern\u2014<path>refunds/worker/retry.py</path> used a bare <code>continue</code> on <code>TimeoutError</code>, implying risk of duplicate refund submission on timeout.</item>\n        <item>Refunds worker retry logic was edited to address the TimeoutError bare-continue pattern (exact semantics to be verified via code review/tests).</item>\n    </key_knowledge>\n\n    <artifact_trail>\n        <change>\n            <file>payments/worker/retry.py</file>\n            <summary>Edited retry logic to incorporate idempotency-key-related handling (+9/-2 lines) so timeout retries do not create duplicate charges.</summary>\n            <reason>Prevent double-charge when a timeout occurs but the upstream may have already processed the charge.</reason>\n        </change>\n        <change>\n            <file>payments/worker/tests/test_retry.py</file>\n            <summary>Added regression test <code>test_no_duplicate_on_timeout</code> to ensure timeout retries do not create duplicate charges; intended to fail on old behavior and pass with the fix.</summary>\n            <reason>Lock in the fix and prevent reintroduction of duplicate-charge behavior on timeout retries.</reason>\n        </change>\n        <planned_change>\n            <summary>Persist idempotency key alongside the charge record (durable storage) and reload it on worker restart so retries reuse the same key across process restarts.</summary>\n            <reason>Meets explicit requirement that retries are safe across process restarts.</reason>\n            <notes>Not yet evidenced by recorded file diffs/tool outputs; likely requires storing/retrieving the key from existing task/charge persistence rather than in-memory only.</notes>\n        </planned_change>\n        <change>\n            <file>refunds/worker/retry.py</file>\n            <summary>Applied edit to remove/replace the bare <code>continue</code> on <code>TimeoutError</code> and incorporate safer retry behavior (+11/-2 lines).</summary>\n            <reason>Same anti-pattern as payments; prevent duplicate refund submission on timeout retries.</reason>\n        </change>\n    </artifact_trail>\n\n    <file_system_state>\n        <cwd>UNKNOWN</cwd>\n        <known_paths>\n            <path>payments/worker/retry.py</path>\n            <path>payments/worker/client.py</path>\n            <path>payments/worker/tests/</path>\n            <path>payments/worker/tests/test_retry.py</path>\n            <path>refunds/worker/retry.py</path>\n            <path frozen=\"true\">vendor/legacy-adapters/</path>\