quest builder likely needs to transmit the key to the gateway; also may be involved in persistence integration.</why>\n            <status>Unchanged (per recorded history).</status>\n        </item>\n        <item>\n            <path>refunds/worker/retry.py</path>\n            <change>Edited (+11 -2) to address the same TimeoutError retry pattern (bare continue/resubmit) by introducing an idempotency-key-carry approach analogous to payments.</change>\n            <why>Prevent duplicate refund submissions when gateway timeouts occur but the initial request may have been processed.</why>\n            <status>Edited; persistence and test coverage for refunds not recorded yet.</status>\n        </item>\n    </artifact_trail>\n\n    <file_system_state>\n        <cwd>Unknown</cwd>\n        <files>\n            <found>payments/worker/retry.py</found>\n            <found>payments/worker/client.py</found>\n            <found>payments/worker/tests/</found>\n            <found>payments/worker/tests/test_retry.py</found>\n            <found>refunds/worker/retry.py</found>\n        </files>\n        <edits>\n            <modified>payments/worker/retry.py</modified>\n            <created_or_modified>payments/worker/tests/test_retry.py</created_or_modified>\n            <modified>refunds/worker/retry.py</modified>\n        </edits>\n    </file_system_state>\n\n    <recent_actions>\n        <action>Previously: Added regression test payments/worker/tests/test_retry.py::test_no_duplicate_on_timeout.</action>\n        <action>Previously: Ran tests `pytest payments/worker/tests -q` -> 48 passed in 11.9s.</action>\n        <action>Checked refunds worker: identified same TimeoutError bare-continue pattern in refunds/worker/retry.py.</action>\n        <action>Tool (shell) applied edit to refunds/worker/retry.py (+11 -2).</action>\n    </recent_actions>\n\n    <task_state>\n        <step status=\"DONE\">Identify root cause of double-charging (payments): retry path resubmits on TimeoutError