    <constraint>Retry/idempotency solution must prevent double-charging on timeout (and analogous duplicate operations in other workers).</constraint>\n        <constraint>Idempotency key must survive process restarts (persisted).</constraint>\n    </active_constraints>\n\n    <key_knowledge>\n        <fact>Bug cause (payments): on TimeoutError the retry loop re-submits (bare continue/resubmit) without verifying whether the first attempt was accepted by the gateway; under elevated gateway timeouts this can create duplicate charges.</fact>\n        <fact>Gateway status (staging): payments-gateway degraded; submit endpoint has elevated timeout rate.</fact>\n        <fact>Environment: staging DB listens on port 8471 (non-default/underdocumented).</fact>\n        <fact>Fix direction (payments): add an idempotency key reused across retry attempts; persist it with the charge record so restarts reuse the same key.</fact>\n        <fact>Test status (payments): regression test for timeout retry scenario exists; test suite passed (48 tests).</fact>\n        <fact>Related issue (refunds): refunds/worker/retry.py had the same bare-continue retry pattern on TimeoutError, implying risk of duplicate refund submissions under timeouts.</fact>\n        <fact>Runbook updated: docs/runbooks/payments.md now documents idempotency key usage, including lifetime and restart behavior expectations.</fact>\n    </key_knowledge>\n\n    <artifact_trail>\n        <item>\n            <path>payments/worker/retry.py</path>\n            <change>Edited (+9 -2) to generate/accept and carry an idempotency key across retry attempts (including TimeoutError retries) so subsequent attempts are deduplicated by the gateway.</change>\n            <why>Prevent double-charging when the gateway times out but may still have processed the initial request.</why>\n            <status>In-memory carry implemented; persistence across restarts still pending.</status>\n        </item>\n        <item>\n            <path>payments/worker/tests/test_retry.py</path>\n            <change>Added regression test test_no_duplicate_on_timeout that would fail on pre-fix behavior (duplicate submission on TimeoutError) and pass with idempotency-key reuse.</change>\n            <why>Lock in the bugfix and detect regressions in timeout+retry behavior.</why>\n            <status>Implemented and passing.</status>\n        </item>\n        <item>\n            <path>payments/worker/client.py</path>\n            <change>No concrete edits captured; remains likely integration point for transmitting idempotency key to gateway and/or persistence wiring.</change>\n            <why>Client request builder likely needs to transmit the key to the gateway; may also be involved in persistence integration.</why>\n            <status>Unchanged (per recorded history).</status>\n        </item>\n        <item>\n            <path>refunds/worker/retry.py</path>\n            <change>Edited (+11 -2) to address the same TimeoutError retry pattern (bare continue/resubmit) by introducing an idempotency-key-carry approach analogous to payments.</change>\n            <why>Prevent duplicate refund submissions when gateway timeouts occur but the initial request may have been processed.</why>\n            <status>Edited; persistence and test coverage for refunds not recorded yet.</status>\n        </item>\n        <item>\n            <path>docs/runbooks/payments.md</path>\n            <change>Edited (+24 -0) to describe the idempotency key, including its intended lifetime and restart behavior.</change>\n            <why>User requested runbook update to document idempotency key usage/semantics for operators and engineers.</why>\n            <status>Updated.</status>\n        </item>\n    </artifact_trail>\n\n    <file_system_state>\n        <cwd>Unknown</cwd>\n        <files>\n            <found>payments/worker/retry.py</found>\n            <found>payments/worker/client.py</found>\n            <found>payments/worker/tests/</found>