etry reuses it rather than minting a fresh one. **Storage layer has not been inspected yet.** Started, unfinished.\n5. **DONE (investigation)** \u2014 Confirmed `refunds/worker/retry.py` has the identical bare `continue` on `TimeoutError`.\n6. **\u26a0\ufe0f DONE BUT UNREQUESTED & UNVERIFIED** \u2014 An edit was applied to `refunds/worker/retry.py` (+11 \u22122). The user only asked to **check** whether the pattern exists, not to fix it. This edit:\n   - was not authorized by the user;\n   - has **no** accompanying test;\n   - has **not** been run against any test suite (refunds tests never executed);\n   - has not been diffed/reviewed for API-shape preservation.\n   **Next assistant must surface this to the user explicitly** \u2014 offer to keep, revert, or review it \u2014 rather than folding it silently into the work.\n\n\u26a0\ufe0f Two separate \"looks done\" traps: the green 48-test run covers payments in-process retry **only**, and the refunds edit is unverified. Neither indicates the overall task is complete. The restart-durability window is still open.\n\n## Remaining Next Steps\n1. **Tell the user about the unrequested refunds edit** and get a decision before building on it.\n2. Finish restart durability (payments): locate charge-record persistence (likely reachable from `payments/worker/client.py`), store the idempotency key with the record.\n3. On worker startup / charge load, read the existing key; generate a new one **only when absent**.\n4. Re-verify `submit_with_retry` signature and return/raise contract unchanged \u2014 `RetryExhausted(charge.id)` behavior and `MAX_ATTEMPTS` / `BACKOFF_SECONDS` semantics intact (explicit user constraint). Apply the same check to the refunds edit.\n5. Add a timeout-then-restart test (same key reused across simulated process restart \u2192 no duplicate). Existing `test_no_duplicate_on_timeout` covers in-process retry only.\n6. Run the refunds test suite if the refunds edit is kept.\n7. **Flag, don't fix silently:** `B