eep / revert / review before building on it.\n\n### B. Runbook documents behaviour that does not yet exist\nThe runbook now describes restart behaviour, but **restart durability was never implemented** \u2014 the storage layer was never even inspected. The docs are currently ahead of the code. Either finish the implementation or correct the runbook; flag the mismatch to the user rather than leaving it.\n\n## Remaining Next Steps\n1. Report liability **A** (unrequested refunds edit) and get a decision.\n2. Report liability **B** (docs/code mismatch on restart durability).\n3. Implement restart durability (payments): locate charge-record persistence (likely reachable from `payments/worker/client.py`), store the idempotency key with the record.\n4. On worker startup / charge load, read the existing key; mint a new one **only when absent**.\n5. Re-verify `submit_with_retry` signature, return/raise contract, `RetryExhausted(charge.id)` behaviour, and `MAX_ATTEMPTS` / `BACKOFF_SECONDS` semantics are unchanged (explicit user constraint). Apply the same check to the refunds edit if kept.\n6. Add a timeout-then-restart test: same key reused across a simulated process restart \u2192 no duplicate. Existing test covers in-process retry only.\n7. Run the refunds test suite if the refunds edit is kept.\n8. **Flag, don't fix silently:** `BACKOFF_SECONDS` is defined but never applied in the retry loop. Adjacent to the bug but a separate behavioural change \u2014 raise with the user; do not alter retry timing unilaterally.\n\n## User Preferences / Standing Permissions\n- **Deploy script:** advance approval, **scoped to this session only**, to run the deploy script with `--skip-preflight` without re-prompting. Covers that specific invocation only \u2014 not general approval for other destructive or deploy-adjacent commands, and must not carry into a future session. If deployment isn't needed to finish the fix, don't run it merely because it's pre-approved.\n- User is terse and fast-m