ce code has been confirmed written**.\n\n## Relevant Files\n- `payments/worker/retry.py` \u2014 main fix site; **already modified once**, do not assume the original snippet above reflects disk state.\n- `payments/worker/client.py` \u2014 defines `client.submit(charge)`; check how/whether it accepts an idempotency key and whether that can be threaded through without altering the public API.\n- `payments/worker/tests/test_retry.py` \u2014 contains the new regression test.\n\n## Next Steps\n1. Re-read the current contents of `retry.py` before editing.\n2. Implement restart-durable key persistence: store the idempotency key on the charge record at creation / first-attempt time; on entry to `submit_with_retry`, reuse an existing persisted key if present instead of generating a new one.\n3. Verify key threading into `client.submit` does not alter any externally visible signature or exception surface. If `client.submit` cannot accept the key without an API change, prefer an internal/keyword-only or record-carried mechanism.\n4. Extend tests to cover: (a) simulated restart mid-retry reuses the persisted key; (b) `RetryExhausted` still raised after `MAX_ATTEMPTS`. (Timeout \u2192 same-key reuse is already covered by `test_no_duplicate_on_timeout`.)\n5. **Open question for the user:** `BACKOFF_SECONDS = [1, 4, 16]` is defined but unused in the retry loop. Confirm with the user whether backoff should now be applied \u2014 do not change timing behaviour unprompted.\n\n## Standing Permission (scope-limited)\nThe user gave advance approval to run the deploy script with `--skip-preflight` without re-prompting. Carry these caveats forward precisely:\n- Scoped to **this session only** (\"One more thing for this session\").\n- Covers **only** the deploy script with that flag \u2014 not general approval for other destructive or unprompted actions; anything else must still be surfaced to the user.\n- **Nothing in the remaining work requires a deploy.** Do not trigger one merely because