ion path.\n        - Idempotency key must survive process restarts (explicit user requirement).\n    </active_constraints>\n\n    <key_knowledge>\n        - Root cause: in `payments/worker/retry.py`, a bare `continue` on `TimeoutError` re-submits the charge without checking whether the first attempt actually landed downstream, producing a duplicate charge.\n        - Chosen remedy: generate an idempotency key once and carry it across all retry attempts so a re-submission is deduplicated.\n        - Charge submission is funneled through a client wrapper (`payments/worker/client.py`), introduced in commit 0ac93f5 \u2014 the key must be threaded through this wrapper.\n        - A retry backoff table exists (commit 41d8e07); timeout handling was recently tightened (commit 9f2c1ab), so the timeout branch is freshly-touched code.\n        - In-memory-only keys are insufficient; persistence must be tied to the charge record so a restarted process reuses the same key.\n    </key_knowledge>\n\n    <artifact_trail>\n        - `payments/worker/retry.py`: Edited (+9 -2) to add an idempotency key carried across retry attempts, replacing the unguarded `continue` on `TimeoutError` that caused double charges.\n        - `payments/worker/client.py`: Identified as the charge submission wrapper (per commit 0ac93f5); expected carrier of the idempotency key to the downstream call. Not yet confirmed modified.\n        - Design decision: dedupe via idempotency key rather than post-timeout status polling, to avoid changing the public API shape.\n        - Design decision (pending implementation): store the idempotency key alongside the charge record for restart durability.\n    </artifact_trail>\n\n    <file_system_state>\n        - Relevant tree: `payments/worker/`\n          - `payments/worker/retry.py` \u2014 MODIFIED (+9 -2), contains the retry/timeout logic and the fix.\n          - `payments/worker/client.py` \u2014 READ/IDENTIFIED, charge submission wrapper.\n          - `payments/w