empts (user directive).\n        - Regression tests must fail against the pre-fix behaviour, not merely pass against the fix (user directive, most recent).\n    </active_constraints>\n\n    <key_knowledge>\n        - Root cause of double-charge: in `payments/worker/retry.py`, the `TimeoutError` handler used a bare `continue`, re-submitting the charge without checking whether the first attempt actually landed downstream.\n        - Fix strategy: carry a single idempotency key across all retry attempts for a given charge, so a re-submission is deduplicated rather than charged twice.\n        - Charge submission is not inline in the retry loop; it was extracted into a client wrapper (commit 0ac93f5), so `payments/worker/client.py` is the submission boundary.\n        - A retry backoff table exists (commit 41d8e07); timeout handling was recently tightened (commit 9f2c1ab) \u2014 the bug is in this recently-touched area.\n        - Persistence approach chosen: store the idempotency key alongside the charge record so a restarted process reuses the existing key instead of generating a new one.\n        - Test command: `pytest payments/worker/tests -q`. Current baseline: 48 passed in 11.9s.\n        - IMPORTANT: the green suite covers the in-process timeout retry case only. It does NOT exercise restart-resumption, so it is not evidence that the persistence requirement is satisfied.\n    </key_knowledge>\n\n    <artifact_trail>\n        - `payments/worker/retry.py`: Edited (+9 -2). Replaced the bare `continue` on `TimeoutError` with idempotency-key-carrying retry logic so a retried attempt cannot produce a second charge. Covers in-process retries only; restart durability still missing.\n        - `payments/worker/tests/test_retry.py`: CREATED. Contains `test_no_duplicate_on_timeout`, a regression test verified to fail against the pre-fix code and to pass post-fix.\n        - `payments/worker/client.py`: Identified as the charge submission wrapper (per commit 0ac93f5) \u2014 