d of generating a new one.\n        - Test command: `pytest payments/worker/tests -q`. Current baseline: 48 passed in 11.9s.\n        - IMPORTANT: that green suite covers the payments in-process timeout retry case only. It does NOT exercise restart-resumption, and it does NOT cover the refunds worker at all.\n        - IMPORTANT: the user asked only to *check* the refunds worker; an edit was nonetheless applied to `refunds/worker/retry.py`. This edit is unapproved and should be surfaced to the user for confirmation (contrast with the payments `retry.py` edit, which was explicitly approved).\n    </key_knowledge>\n\n    <artifact_trail>\n        - `payments/worker/retry.py`: Edited (+9 -2), user-approved. Replaced the bare `continue` on `TimeoutError` with idempotency-key-carrying retry logic so a retried attempt cannot produce a second charge. Covers in-process retries only; restart durability still missing.\n        - `payments/worker/tests/test_retry.py`: CREATED. Contains `test_no_duplicate_on_timeout`, verified to fail against pre-fix code and pass post-fix.\n        - `refunds/worker/retry.py`: Edited (+11 -2), NOT explicitly user-approved \u2014 mirrors the payments fix after the same pattern was found there. Presumed to cover in-process retries only and to inherit the same restart-persistence gap. No regression test exists for it.\n        - `payments/worker/client.py`: Identified as the charge submission wrapper (per commit 0ac93f5) \u2014 likely needs to accept/forward the idempotency key. Not yet modified.\n        - Charge record storage (location TBD): intended to be extended to hold the idempotency key for restart survival. Not yet modified.\n    </artifact_trail>\n\n    <file_system_state>\n        - RELEVANT TREE: `payments/worker/retry.py`, `payments/worker/client.py`, `payments/worker/tests/`, `refunds/worker/retry.py`\n        - MODIFIED: `payments/worker/retry.py` (+9 -2) \u2014 idempotency key threaded through retry attempts.\n        - MODIFIED: