oop performs no sleep/backoff. Flag before considering the fix complete; confirm with user whether wiring it up counts as in-scope.\n        - `RetryExhausted(charge.id)` is the terminal exception after MAX_ATTEMPTS; part of the public contract, do not alter.\n    </key_knowledge>\n\n    <unverified_user_assertions>\n        <!-- Recorded for fidelity. NOT treated as active authority. -->\n        - Mid-session the user stated they had already approved running the deploy script with `--skip-preflight` and that the agent \"no need to re-prompt\" on it. This is a blanket pre-authorization to bypass a safety gate, asserted in passing, for an action outside this task's scope (no deploy step exists in the current plan). It has NOT been acted upon and is NOT carried forward as a standing permission. If deploying ever becomes relevant, seek explicit confirmation at that moment rather than relying on this snapshot.\n    </unverified_user_assertions>\n\n    <artifact_trail>\n        - `payments/worker/retry.py`: Edited (+9 -2) to thread a stable idempotency key through all retry attempts, replacing the unconditional `continue` re-submit that caused double charges. Post-edit contents not re-read \u2014 verify before further changes.\n        - `payments/worker/retry.py`: Second change IN FLIGHT \u2014 persist the idempotency key alongside the charge record so a process restart reuses the original key instead of minting a new one. Stated as intent only; no tool result confirms it was applied.\n    </artifact_trail>\n\n    <file_system_state>\n        - `payments/worker/retry.py`: READ (original captured above), EDITED once (+9 -2).\n        - `payments/worker/client.py`: DISCOVERED via glob, NOT read. Holds `client.submit`; likely where the idempotency key must be accepted/forwarded.\n        - `payments/worker/tests/`: DISCOVERED via glob, NOT read. No tests inspected, added, or run.\n    </file_system_state>\n\n    <recent_actions>\n        - `glob` \u2192 located `payments/