sk).\n        - Idempotency key must survive process restarts, not just live in memory for the duration of a retry loop.\n    </active_constraints>\n\n    <key_knowledge>\n        - Root cause of double-charge: in `payments/worker/retry.py`, a bare `continue` on `TimeoutError` re-submits the charge without checking whether the first attempt actually landed.\n        - Fix strategy: carry an idempotency key across all retry attempts so a re-submission is deduplicated rather than charged twice.\n        - Charge submission was extracted into a client wrapper (commit `0ac93f5`), so `payments/worker/client.py` is the likely path the key must thread through.\n        - Recent git history is concentrated in this area: `9f2c1ab` Tighten timeout handling in payments worker; `41d8e07` Add retry backoff table; `0ac93f5` Extract charge submission into client wrapper.\n        - A retry backoff table exists (`41d8e07`) and is part of the retry path's existing behavior.\n    </key_knowledge>\n\n    <artifact_trail>\n        - `payments/worker/retry.py`: Edit applied (+9 -2). Replaced the unguarded `continue`-on-`TimeoutError` behavior with an idempotency key carried across retry attempts, so a timed-out attempt that actually landed is not charged again.\n        - `payments/worker/client.py`: Not yet modified. Holds the extracted charge-submission wrapper; expected to need the idempotency key plumbed through without changing its public signature semantics.\n        - Persistence of the idempotency key alongside the charge record: stated as the intended approach for restart durability, NOT yet confirmed written to any file.\n    </artifact_trail>\n\n    <file_system_state>\n        - Relevant tree (from glob):\n          - `payments/worker/retry.py` \u2014 MODIFIED (+9 -2), contains the retry loop and the bug fix so far.\n          - `payments/worker/client.py` \u2014 EXISTS, not yet read or modified.\n          - `payments/worker/tests/` \u2014 EXISTS, contents not yet inspected